co4fe3 contains no third-party source code other than its declared npm dependencies.

Its design is informed by the following open source projects. Ideas, parameters and architecture were studied and
reimplemented in co4fe3's own code; no code was copied from them.

- V3Code, Copyright (c) 2025-2026 KandD Labs, Apache License 2.0.
  https://github.com/HeavenFYouMissed/V3Code, studied at commit 2eac91fb.
  Ideas: runtime policy (repeat thresholds, consecutive-mistake stop), modes derived from approval categories,
  research/work subagent profiles, evidence-checked worker outcomes, Reciprocal Rank Fusion retrieval with a
  latency budget, the LSP-backed context pack and its per-task caps, verify-against-baseline after an edit,
  monotonic draft run states, project instruction and skill loading. "V3Code" is a trademark of KandD Labs;
  co4fe3 is not affiliated with it.
- Void Editor, Copyright Void Editor contributors, Apache License 2.0. https://github.com/voideditor/void
  Ideas: streamed per-diff review and search/replace edits (via V3Code).
- Cline, Copyright (c) Cline Bot Inc., Apache License 2.0. https://github.com/cline/cline
  Ideas: tool approval flow, checkpoints.
- Aider, Apache License 2.0. https://github.com/Aider-AI/aider
  Ideas: repository map ranked by a reference graph, search/replace edit format.
- Continue, Copyright (c) Continue Dev, Inc., Apache License 2.0. https://github.com/continuedev/continue
  Ideas: @-mentions, context providers.
